    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "SLEM-05-231025 - SLEM 5 file systems that are being imported via Network File System (NFS) must be mounted to prevent files with the setuid and setgid bit set from being executed."
      info        : "The \"nosuid\" mount option causes the system to not execute \"setuid\" and \"setgid\" files with owner privileges. This option must be used for mounting any file system not containing approved \"setuid\" and \"setguid\" files. Executing files from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for unprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access."
      solution    : "Configure SLEM 5 \"/etc/fstab\" file to use the \"nosuid\" option on file systems that are being exported via NFS."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,DISA_Benchmark|SLEM_5_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-261281r996326_rule,STIG-ID|SLEM-05-231025,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-261281"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_SLEM_5_V1R4_STIG.zip"
      file        : "/etc/fstab"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*[^#\\n\\r]*[\\s]+nfs([2-4])?[\\s]+"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*[^#\\n\\r]*[\\s]+nfs([2-4])?[\\s]+[^#\\n\\r]*nosuid"
      required    : NO
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
