    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "SLEM-05-651015 - SLEM 5 file integrity tool must be configured to verify Access Control Lists (ACLs)."
      info        : "ACLs can provide permissions beyond those permitted through the file mode and must be verified by file integrity tools.

NOTE: Nessus has provided the target output to assist in reviewing the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "Configure SLEM 5 file integrity tool to check file and directory ACLs.

If AIDE is installed, ensure the \"acl\" rule is present on all file and directory selection lists."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,DISA_Benchmark|SLEM_5_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-261404r996629_rule,STIG-ID|SLEM-05-651015,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-261404"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_SLEM_5_V1R4_STIG.zip"
      cmd         : "/bin/echo 'Uncommented selection lines with out acl:'; /bin/grep -E \"^\s*[\\/\\!\\=]\" /etc/aide.conf | /bin/grep -vi acl"
      expect      : "^Manual Review Required$"
      severity    : MEDIUM
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "SLEM-05-651020 - SLEM 5 file integrity tool must be configured to verify extended attributes."
      info        : "Extended attributes in file systems are used to contain arbitrary data and file metadata with security implications.

NOTE: Nessus has provided the target output to assist in reviewing the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "Configure SLEM 5 file integrity tool to check file and directory extended attributes.

If AIDE is installed, ensure the \"xattrs\" rule is present on all file and directory selection lists."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,DISA_Benchmark|SLEM_5_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-261405r996631_rule,STIG-ID|SLEM-05-651020,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-261405"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_SLEM_5_V1R4_STIG.zip"
      cmd         : "/bin/echo 'Uncommented selection lines with out xattrs:'; /bin/grep -E \"^\s*[\\/\\!\\=]\" /etc/aide.conf | /bin/grep -vi xattrs"
      expect      : "^Manual Review Required$"
      severity    : MEDIUM
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "aide.conf auditd"
          file        : "/etc/aide.conf"
          regex       : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/auditd[\\s]*"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/auditd[\\s]*p\\+i\\+n\\+u\\+g\\+s\\+b\\+acl\\+selinux\\+xattrs\\+sha512"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "aide.conf augenrules"
          file        : "/etc/aide.conf"
          regex       : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/augenrules[\\s]*"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/augenrules[\\s]*p\\+i\\+n\\+u\\+g\\+s\\+b\\+acl\\+selinux\\+xattrs\\+sha512"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "aide.conf audispd"
          file        : "/etc/aide.conf"
          regex       : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/audispd[\\s]*"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/audispd[\\s]*p\\+i\\+n\\+u\\+g\\+s\\+b\\+acl\\+selinux\\+xattrs\\+sha512"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "aide.conf auditctl"
          file        : "/etc/aide.conf"
          regex       : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/auditctl[\\s]*"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/auditctl[\\s]*p\\+i\\+n\\+u\\+g\\+s\\+b\\+acl\\+selinux\\+xattrs\\+sha512"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "aide.conf aureport"
          file        : "/etc/aide.conf"
          regex       : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/aureport[\\s]*"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/aureport[\\s]*p\\+i\\+n\\+u\\+g\\+s\\+b\\+acl\\+selinux\\+xattrs\\+sha512"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "aide.conf ausearch"
          file        : "/etc/aide.conf"
          regex       : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/ausearch[\\s]*"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/ausearch[\\s]*p\\+i\\+n\\+u\\+g\\+s\\+b\\+acl\\+selinux\\+xattrs\\+sha512"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "aide.conf autrace"
          file        : "/etc/aide.conf"
          regex       : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/autrace[\\s]*"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*/usr/sbin/autrace[\\s]*p\\+i\\+n\\+u\\+g\\+s\\+b\\+acl\\+selinux\\+xattrs\\+sha512"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "SLEM-05-651025 - SLEM 5 file integrity tool must be configured to protect the integrity of the audit tools."
          info        : "Protecting the integrity of the tools used for auditing purposes is a critical step toward ensuring the integrity of audit information. Audit information includes all information (e.g., audit records, audit settings, and audit reports) needed to successfully audit information system activity.

Audit tools include but are not limited to vendor-provided and open-source audit tools needed to successfully view and manipulate audit information system activity and records. Audit tools include custom queries and report generators.

It is not uncommon for attackers to replace the audit tools or inject code into the existing tools to provide the capability to hide or erase system activity from the audit logs.

To address this risk, audit tools must be cryptographically signed to provide the capability to identify when the audit tools have been modified, manipulated, or replaced. An example is a checksum hash of the file or files."
          solution    : "Configure SLEM 5 file integrity tool to protect the integrity of the audit tools.

Add or modify the following lines in the \"/etc/aide.conf\" file:

# audit tools
/usr/sbin/auditctl p+i+n+u+g+s+b+acl+selinux+xattrs+sha512
