        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "SLEM-05-654185 - SLEM 5 must generate audit records for all uses of the \"umount\" system call."
          info        : "Reconstruction of harmful events or forensic analysis is not possible if audit records do not contain enough information.

At a minimum, the organization must audit the full-text recording of privileged commands. The organization must maintain audit trails in sufficient detail to reconstruct events to determine the cause and impact of compromise."
          solution    : "Configure SLEM 5 to generate an audit record for all uses of the \"umount\" and \"umount2\" system calls.

Add or modify the following lines in the \"/etc/audit/rules.d/audit.rules\" file:

-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -S umount -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=unset -k privileged-umount
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -S umount2 -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=unset -k privileged-umount
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S umount2 -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=unset -k privileged-umount

To reload the rules file, restart the audit daemon:

     > sudo systemctl restart auditd.service

or issue the following command:

     > sudo augenrules --load"
